ksh93: the current directory has one leading slash where HOME is /.

Amix has no getcwd system call, so libast's getcwd walks up the tree,
and stops early at a directory it knows from $PWD or $HOME, putting
that path in front. Root's HOME is "/", and in front of "var/pk" it gave
"//var/pk": $PWD, ${.sh.file} and script paths began with two slashes.
"/" is not taken as such a directory; the walk ends at the root.

--- a/programs/dtksh/ksh93/src/lib/libast/misc/getcwd.c
+++ b/programs/dtksh/ksh93/src/lib/libast/misc/getcwd.c
@@ -298,7 +298,8 @@
 		closedir(dirp);
 		dirp = 0;
 		for (n = 0; n < elementsof(env); n++)
-			if (env[n].ino == par->st_ino && env[n].dev == par->st_dev)
+			/* not "/" (root's HOME), which gave "//dir": the walk ends at the root */
+			if (env[n].ino == par->st_ino && env[n].dev == par->st_dev && env[n].path[1])
 			{
 				namlen = strlen(env[n].path);
 				goto found;
